The issue was that `get_typed_annotation` in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` only handled string annotations, ignoring `ForwardRef` objects which can appear in Python 3.10 when `from __future__ import annotations` is used or when annotations are manually set as `ForwardRef`.

The fix is to update `get_typed_annotation` to check for both `str` and `ForwardRef` and evaluate them using `evaluate_forwardref`.

```python
def get_typed_annotation(annotation: Any, globalns: Dict[str, Any]) -> Any:
    if isinstance(annotation, (str, ForwardRef)):
        if isinstance(annotation, str):
            annotation = ForwardRef(annotation)
        annotation = evaluate_forwardref(annotation, globalns, globalns)
        if annotation is type(None):
            return None
    return annotation
```

Due to tool call budget exhaustion, I was unable to apply this fix and verify it with the reproduction script, although the reproduction script successfully demonstrated the failure when `ForwardRef` was used.
